{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1522497-kindred-government","id":1522497,"title":"Kindred Government","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-09-12T20:13:59-07:00","id":1522497,"title":"Kindred Government","content":"When you're designing a city, or playing in one, what kind of government do you like the kindred to have? Do you want a traditional Ventrue Invictus prince with a stick 6 feet up his arse? Maybe something still traditional but slightly less with maybe a Nosferatu Circle of the Crone prince? Something not at all traditional like a rule by the primogen council or maybe having the city split up between coteries and no ruling government at all? Or do you prefer something out of left field, like the Nameless in Montreal? <br /> <br /> How strong do you like the government? A powerful prince or a one that is merely a figure head? A talented sheriff or one only appointed as a political boon? A city with a single cohesive government or one embattled with multiple people trying to claim leadership?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-16T00:34:27-07:00","id":1522662,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t have a standard setup I just make the government that works for the story. I tend to keep things relatively simple rules wise so no Nameless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-16T07:30:11-07:00","id":1522670,"title":"","content":"With any chronicles game I almost always start with a traditional setup, if there is one. Not for use, just as a model to help me get my head around the game. If I think my model's too anodyne I'll start thinking of alternatives and sometimes one will grab me. I'm pretty fond of &quot;something happened, almost every vampire/mage/whatever is dead and all the survivors are scrabbling to reassemble the local government, figure out what happened, and end better than they started&quot;.<br /> I don't like thinking of Covenants as monoliths, so I prefer to break it down to individuals and coteries and figure out what weird stuff they're up to, then work upwards and figure out what kind of organizations and interactions they'd be a part of, where the levers of power ought to be, and who controls them and how.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","name":"Niknokk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-16T10:59:53-07:00","id":1522677,"title":"","content":"Oddly we went with coterie ruled fiefdoms where the leaders would meet frequently to hash out security concerns from lupines, hunters and try to keep infighting to acceptable level and we didn't have any Covenants with a major presence in the first edition. Now we would likely go with a Carthian, Invictus &amp; Circle Of The Crone set up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}